{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>When one comes</b> — a hint to the day of birth." "<b>When contempt also comes</b> — with it, that one may scorn others; and with disgrace, that one may disgrace them; insult comes, that one may insult them. And the meaning: disgrace drags insult, as in the matter of \"one transgression drags another.\""], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:23:27.492611016Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}